    "updated_at": "2026-10-27T18:19:39Z",
    "seo": {
      "title": "Dotin: Iranian Banking Software and Core Systems | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Explore Dotin's published banking-software portfolio, centralized processing model and migration work, with clear distinctions between claims and verified outcomes."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "company-role",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Infrastructure and customer-facing products",
        "content": "Dotin describes its business as supplying infrastructure to financial institutions while also developing technology-based financial products for end users. Its corporate introduction identifies banking and insurance software alongside Wepod, which it describes as Bank Pasargad's digital banking service. This places the company across institutional infrastructure and customer-facing product development. [s1]\n\nThe company frames its mission around financial inclusion, particularly access for people in smaller towns and rural areas. That is a statement of purpose. Demonstrating whether access has improved would require evidence about who uses the services, who remains excluded and how outcomes differ across locations. The corporate introduction alone does not establish those results. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "banking-offering",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "What Dotin calls comprehensive banking",
        "content": "Dotin uses the Persian term for a comprehensive banking solution to describe its core-banking offering. Its product page emphasizes tailoring software to a bank's operating scale, branch network, customer mix and strategic requirements. It also describes configurable parameters through which banks can define products without changing application code. These are published capabilities, rather than findings from an independent technical evaluation. [s2]\n\nThe rial core product provides a more specific architectural description: banking information is stored and processed centrally rather than maintained through separate branch-centred systems. Its listed features include event-driven operation, integration with surrounding systems and customization. The page does not establish the configuration running at every customer institution. [s3]",
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s3"]
      },
      {
        "id": "portfolio-boundaries",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A portfolio is broader than the account system",
        "content": "Dotin's comprehensive banking page lists internet and mobile banking, card management, a banking switch, data warehousing, fraud detection and anti-money-laundering software alongside its core products. Anti-money-laundering software supports the identification and investigation of potentially suspicious activity; listing such a product does not demonstrate that financial crime has been prevented. The portfolio also includes data migration and infrastructure services. [s2]\n\nFor an international reader, these distinctions help explain the supplier's role. A core product, a customer channel and an analytical application address different functions, even when sold by the same company. The catalogue should therefore be read as a set of offerings, not as proof that every listed function has been deployed together at a particular bank. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "migration-experience",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Migration as an organizational project",
        "content": "A first-person project account published under Dotin's name on Virgool describes its work on Bank Sepah's move toward centralized banking. The account separates infrastructure and security, migration, training, gap analysis, implementation and operation into distinct workstreams. It also describes specialist groups within the bank and corresponding supplier teams. [s4]\n\nThis account is useful because it shows how the supplier presents the work beyond software installation: business analysis and staff preparation sit alongside technical changes. It remains participant testimony. Independent bank-side acceptance records, incident evidence and customer-experience research would be needed to assess the migration's wider results. This profile consequently describes the documented offering and reported project approach without assigning Dotin a performance ranking.",
        "source_ids": ["s4"]
      }
    ],
